{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1253461-contracts-for-combat","id":1253461,"title":"Contracts for Combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-11T20:02:19-07:00","id":1253461,"title":"Contracts for Combat","content":"I'm pretty new to Changeling: The Lost's 2nd Edition and had introduced a Huntsman and Changeling into the game I'm running, but the PC kinda pulled the trigger on starting a fight with the Huntsman before I was really ready for it.<br /> <br /> Can I get some advice on what Contracts or other supernatural powers might be effective in producing a dangerous Huntsman?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T20:19:21-07:00","id":1253463,"title":"","content":"Tell us more about the situation the Huntsman is stuck in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T20:44:17-07:00","id":1253468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1253461-contracts-for-combat?p=1253463#post1253463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell us more about the situation the Huntsman is stuck in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whew, okay, well... I'm not sure exactly where to start this, so I'll just explain how the scene got to where it is, if it'll help, and then the PCs capabilities.<br /> <br /> The game is focused on a Beast (from Beast: The Primordial) who was introduced to a Changeling by hitting them with his car on a rainy night. The Changeling was newly escaped from Arcadia with a Huntsman in pursuit. The Beast knew they didn't really know what was going on, just that they'd injured a terrified teenager who smelled of Kinship and was trying to warn him away from getting involved. A crow was noticed then that acted oddly (really a faerie falcon of the Huntsman for tracking purposes) and the Beast decided to get involved, throwing a knife that injured the bird and causing it to fly away. The Beast convinced the Changeling to get into his car and they drove off, with the Beast asking some questions. The Changeling could've continued running, but after seeing that the Huntsman's falcon was injured, he's worried about the Beast suffering repercussions for that. At some point, they stop at a gas station so that the Beast could make a personal call to someone about a personal responsibility, when the Huntsman shows up at the gas station as a man walking a bunch of dogs (really faerie hounds).<br /> <br /> So, the current situation is the Beast staring down the Huntsman at the gas station, where the Huntsman has tried offering some kind of deal with the Beast in exchange for the Changeling to be handed over. The Huntsman recognizes the Beast as some kind of supernatural entity and I played up the Thicker Than Water showing the Huntsman having a good impression to offer some non-violent means to resolve their differences. However, that didn't really sit well with the Beast, and now he's worried about the Huntsman possibly targeting him for interfering and so wants to start the fight now.<br /> <br /> For the current environment, the Beast was able to trigger Lair Traits and open a Primordial Pathway in the area. Also, the Beast has Cyclopean Strength, Relentless Hunter, Unbreakable and Limb From Limb, kind of making him a real combat terror from my understanding of the rules.<br /> <br /> My preferred goal here would be to have a Huntsman who can give an interesting and credible fight for the Beast, and better show that there are things out there that can hurt him. If the Huntsman can last for the four rounds until the Primordial Pathway closes, that is fine, and I can have the Huntsman retreat then to stalk his real prey later. If the Huntsman gets killed, I'm okay with that outcome (and can think of consequences for it later), but would really prefer it's not an immediate KO.<br /> <br /> Does that help explain the situation better?<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, the Huntsman tore his Mask away and I described him as having fancy leather armor and a spear as a weapon. But nothing is really defined on what that stuff can do yet. And the Lair Traits in effect are Blizzard, Extreme Cold and Razored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 09-12-2018, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T21:30:21-07:00","id":1253482,"title":"","content":"A verderer is made for hunting, not head-to-head combat. They are built to be scary for their capacity to be anywhere and look like anybody and ignore the weaknesses common to the fae and act as the manifest will of one of the most personally terrifying things in specific changelings' lives. They are seldom operating on such a tight time limit that they can't afford to pick their moment and regroup later. Every Huntsman is effectively a high-Potency fae Horror with no frailties, immunity to iron, relatively unlimited humanoid shapeshifting, the ability to turn predators into proxies, and regularly-accessible gear that gives them 8-Again to use it and lets them recover Willpower when they do so.<br /> <br /> The scope of available Dread Powers is such that you can customize a Huntsman about as thoroughly as you can any hobgoblin, and the specific wheelhouse of the Huntsmen includes power options that are specifically troublesome for changelings, like ferreting out their Touchstones or inflicting Paranoid or <i>just showing up out of nowhere</i>. Making use of less specialized Dread Powers opens up yet more options \u2014 a Huntsman with Reality Stutter or Mist Form Immortal or Hypnotic Gaze or Lethe's Embrace provides its own forms of threat even if it isn't sporting a sledgehammer of exceptional quality.<br /> <br /> The defensive game for Huntsmen is basically identical to the defensive game for changelings: Avoid damage by not being there when the check bounces. What Title does this Huntsman bear?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-12-2018, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T21:50:07-07:00","id":1253488,"title":"","content":"The Huntsman's Title I used is &quot;The Patient Stalker&quot;. The Huntsman thought he could make a deal and didn't expect to get turned on so hard. As far as the Huntsman could know, the Changeling could've given the Beast &quot;the wrong ideas&quot; as to what is going on, and thought working out a deal with the monster could reasonably be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T22:33:24-07:00","id":1253496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1253461-contracts-for-combat?p=1253488#post1253488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Huntsman's Title I used is &quot;The Patient Stalker&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you've written yourself into a corner here, because it's entirely common for a Huntsman to wait weeks before they make an open move on their target, and this is the Title poured into the verderer that represents a Fae's desire to recover this changeling that escaped very recently?<br /> <br /> This is a bigger gaffe than needing to have the thing survive for four turns to get away \u2014 this is the sort of thing that seems to warrant a quiet retcon of &quot;this hunter was a servant of the real Huntsman sent to feel out uncertain elements in the early stages of the hunt&quot; if you can manage it, because even if the Stalker is a very weak Huntsman it's probably smart enough not to make such an immediate blunder personally.<br /> <br /> The jump to dealmaking suggests you could get away with calling it a hobgoblin lieutenant, if that's your speed; access to Contracts (especially Goblin Contracts) opens up more options for showcasing the ways a Beast new to handling the fae can be in for a wild time.<br /> <br /> As it stands, I'd lean on the fact that you've established multiple opponents and have the hounds occupy the Beast while the Stalker either goes after the changeling or gathers data and effects an escape; none of the Lair Traits in play are unavoidable, unless I've misread the situational breakdown. What's the Beast's Lair rating and current Satiety?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T23:12:21-07:00","id":1253500,"title":"","content":"Let me clarify my position a little here... I'm not really worried about this particular Huntsman surviving or not. I think it can be fitting for a faerie to be overconfident in their approach, especially in a situation where they think they have an idea of what might be going on, and even more so if they think there's a chance they can get what they want. It's unfortunate for this faerie that he had to proposition an uncompromising monster and might very well get eaten for it.<br /> <br /> The idea of making him an expendable servant isn't a bad one.<br /> <br /> But I think this is getting away a bit from what I'm really trying to find here, which is better understanding of what Contracts are suitable for combat (the variety of Contracts is pretty staggering, with various effects in each category...) and what can really make a faerie fighter scary in combat... and where I just don't have any understanding of those things yet at all. And so, that's really what I intended the thread for, to see if anyone has a solid grasp of those mechanics and might be able to share some insights, so I could be more thoughtful in my approach on building a more interesting scene for my player.<br /> <br /> So far... The best idea I've got is using Whispers of Morning for the faerie to just eye this giant ice wolf bearing down on him and going, &quot;NOPE!&quot; right to being immaterial. And that seems like a Contract that The Patient Stalker would have in their repertoire. And while that would probably be a very smart thing to do.... It wouldn't necessarily make for the most dramatic of a scene. I'm still considering what could be done, such as perhaps using Whispers of Morning to reposition while the faerie hounds hassle the Beast, and then try to kidnap the Changeling, which sounds like a more interesting and active approach...<br /> <br /> However, my interest in learning better what Contracts are impactful in combat and so forth doesn't really change from that.<br /> <br /> (Also, the Beast is at Lair 2, and Satiety 4.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T23:50:11-07:00","id":1253508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1253461-contracts-for-combat?p=1253500#post1253500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, my interest in learning better what Contracts are impactful in combat and so forth doesn't really change from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a separate problem: Huntsman specifically don't have Contracts. They are not the foe to use for showing off the full scope of a fae combatant's potential danger in the mortal world, because their powerset is geared specifically toward finding an exploiting the Lost's fears and vulnerabilities. Outside of their particular Dread Powers, the threat they pose is one that works more like a competent and informed but mundane character than an overtly magical actor outside the Hedge.<br /> <br /> That being said, as a character in a game dealing with a Beast, it's probably appropriate for a Huntsman to have some of its Merit dots allocated to Killer Instinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T11:37:50-07:00","id":1253653,"title":"","content":"Alright, so are there good examples of Dread Powers for designing particularly dangerous combatants?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm still curious about good potential combat oriented Contracts, considering there are Changelings in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 09-12-2018, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T19:48:07-07:00","id":1253776,"title":"","content":"In terms of a straight slugfest Natural Weapons gives the creature +1 damage and +1 armor piercing to a maximum of 3. Unbreakable (the dread power, not the atavism) makes them nearly immune to damage unless the attacker rolls an exceptional success. If that's too powerful/swingy for you (and Cyclopean Strength might render it useless if the Beast is Lair 3+), Werewolf had a Natural Armor dread power that was 1-3 dots of armor.<br /> <br /> Changeling has some pretty powerful combat contracts. Red Revenge is a massive physical buff (+3 to physical attributes, 3/3 armor, among others) with the downside of not being able to focus on anything except attacking the nearest living thing. Talon and Wing grants easy access to agg damage if the Changeling already has lethal unarmed (possibly from the 2 dot Lethal Mien merit). Elemental Weapon can be really, really potent. It creates a weapon from a nearby element, which has the regular stats of its kind plus an extra buff to damage, initiative or range per success. With a good roll you can arm yourself with a +5 sword that... shoots fireballs or something? I'm not sure how adding 20 feet of range works with a melee weapon, I'm imagining the sword lasers from Zelda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T20:30:51-07:00","id":1253785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1253461-contracts-for-combat?p=1253776#post1253776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a good roll you can arm yourself with a +5 sword that... shoots fireballs or something? I'm not sure how adding 20 feet of range works with a melee weapon, I'm imagining the sword lasers from Zelda.</div> </div> </div> </div>A common-sense reading would suggest that you're not picking a melee weapon if you're adding range. Recall that this is still a Common Contract. Burning hatchets and fiery daggers are more in line with the fiction than a good roll on a relatively basic bit of fae pactwork allowing you to instantiate the Master Sword out of everyday stage hazards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T22:24:59-07:00","id":1253811,"title":"","content":"Besides the direct combat powers already mentioned, changelings have access to a number of Contracts meant to make combat a non-issue or tilt things in their favor through trickery. Paralyzing Presence inflicts the Insensate Tilt, Unravel the Tapestry gives you a second chance at avoiding death, and Leaping Toward Nightfall simply neutralizes an assailant for a few days. Might of the Terrible Brute drains an opponent's Strength (or Dexterity if you're a Beast), while The Royal Court stops combat from happening in the first place. The Common Spring Contract Dreams of the Earth puts a target to sleep for a few minutes--time enough to set up a coup de grace. Or you could use the various emotion-manipulating powers of Court Contracts to make your target not want to fight you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T01:41:30-07:00","id":1253829,"title":"","content":"I'd probably have the Huntsman start directing Heroes at the Beast, rather than try and engage in direct combat with them. Especially with those particular atavisms, and doubly so if they bought up their Lair as well. What you absolutely do <i>not</i> want to do is get with in arms reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T09:26:41-07:00","id":1253918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1253461-contracts-for-combat?p=1253829#post1253829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably have the Huntsman start directing Heroes at the Beast, rather than try and engage in direct combat with them. Especially with those particular atavisms, and doubly so if they bought up their Lair as well. What you absolutely do <i>not</i> want to do is get with in arms reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus it gives a nice sense of escalation. Start off harassed by either the Huntsman's agents, or Heroes, then (after a short reprieve) find out they teamed up and are combining forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T11:27:43-07:00","id":1253966,"title":"","content":"To be fair, creatures of the CoD probably don't have metagame knowledge that we have when meeting new creatures. This is the first time the Hunter has met a Beast, he may sense it is supernatural but probably doesn't know what it can do... He may be thinking the Best is just like a common hobgoblin so that might be the reason for his overconfidence attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","name":"Pluvinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T12:07:31-07:00","id":1253970,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggestions, folks!<br /> <br /> Had the session for the fight with the Huntsman and his pack of hounds. I ended up going with the suggestion of using Killer Instinct for aggression and Reality Stutter for defense, but also picked up Spear and Bayonet from Hurt Locker, with another Dread Power being Entangling Snare. The Hounds I gave a couple dots of Natural Weaponry to help with the Armor to keep them a threat.<br /> <br /> The general strategy was for the Hounds to harry the Beast, taking turns to either grapple with the Beast or chip away at him, giving time for the Huntsman to ready up Killer Instinct and drive a powerful strike, with the Huntsman using Entangling Snare if the Hounds have trouble landing a successful grapple. I didn't expect the Hounds to KEEP the Beast grappled, but merely occupy his action constantly. My general goal of this fight was to inflict a serious wound on the Beast and see if he'd consider retreating. I wasn't going to make the Huntsman chase the Beast down or anything. The theme for this was a very... hunting... kind of theme for how this Huntsman approaches combat and I thought it fit the idea of a Patient Stalker moving in for the kill.<br /> <br /> As to how things turned out... Combat lasted for two turns, basically.<br /> <br /> The Beast, who until this point had only engaged with more mundane combatants are saw himself as being bulletproof from what he's seen so far, lunges forward with an All-Out Attack, which.... invited a lot of nastiness from Spear and Bayonet... The Huntsman Reality Stuttered which helped drive down the Beast's dice pool and... the Beast got a dramatic failure, suffering the Knocked Down Tilt for it. And then the Huntsman retaliated with an attack and... the dice just exploded on me with 9 successes (I'm reminded again of how powerful 8-again is...). The Beast took his first Lethal damage since he's come into his true nature and started bleeding. Meanwhile, the Hounds attacked, with a little chip damage.<br /> <br /> The Beast attacked while prone, since the Huntsman's Defense was down, and managed to land a hit with an exceptional success after spending Satiety for Limb From Limb, inflicting an Arm Wrack that just tore off the Huntsman's arm, nearly killing the Huntsman in one big bite. I had the Huntsman react really cautiously to that, planning on having him use Entangling Snare on the Beast next turn as the Huntsman recovered, with the Hounds harassing again. One of the Hounds lands a grapple... but the Beast reacts by winning control of the grapple and flinging the Hound at the Huntsman, clipping him.<br /> <br /> At this point, the Huntsman dramatically failed a perception check.... And that's when I had the Changeling who was hiding in the Beast's car get behind the steering wheel, put the car into reverse and backed the vehicle right over the Huntsman. The Huntsman was completely blindsided from focusing on the Beast and with a loud THUMP, the fight was over. The Beast ended up giving the Changeling a thumbs up.<br /> <br /> With the Primordial Pathway fading away, the Beast was left bleeding from his wound wondering how that spear hurt him so badly and then passed out from the blood loss before his speedy healing could recover him (the player knew he could spend Satiety to stay up, but wanted a Beat and I'm a sucker for trades like that). Later, the Beast woke up at a shelter/freehold the Changeling got him to, and that's how I've introduced him to one of the major players of the local Changeling community.<br /> <br /> Oh, and they jacked the Huntsman's spear. I'm sure he'll be happy about that...<br /> <br /> All in all, I thought it was a pretty successful session. The combat was extremely swingy in just two turns. The Huntsman got burned for being too overconfident, but so did the Beast and I rather like that mirroring. On top of this, the Changeling the Beast helped looks like a solid candidate for Family Ties.<br /> <br /> Better yet, the player enjoyed it!<br /> <br /> So thanks for the help and suggestions. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T12:12:24-07:00","id":1253971,"title":"","content":"As an aside, I'm having the supernatural communities rather segregated from each other in this setting. They're just too focused on themselves and their own worries. Where supernatural entities &quot;cross the streams&quot; are probably going to be Plot Points for the setting.<br /> <br /> The intent for this, is to help the player of the Beast kind of feel like a nexus point for cross-community interaction, as well as to give the Beast a more broad view as to what is going on with the over all supernatural setting. It's to help that character feel more like they're the ones reaching out and making connections that leads to better understanding of what might need to happen in order to resolve conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}